   "summary": "In a Traditional Web module (WebResponsive) a screen is `IWebScreen` in `IWebFlow:MainFlow`, born with its layout web block instance (`$scr/#IWebBlockInstanceWidget/Title|MainContent`); its data is fetched in the Preparation (a logic element), not by lifecycle events; widgets are the web widgets (ui.traditional-widget); a button OnClick has a Destination (a screen action or a screen) and a link OnClick also has a Method. Library blocks (OutSystemsUIWeb) are instanced with `create IWebBlockInstanceWidget` + `source: IWebBlock:<Name>` + `empty`. Emails are IWebEmail. Nothing here applies to Reactive/Mobile or to ODC.",
   "route": {
    "kind": "job",
    "operation": "create IWebScreen in IWebFlow:<Flow>; create IPreparation (logic) under it; create web widgets under $scr/#IWebBlockInstanceWidget/<Placeholder>; set <widget>/OnClick Destination; create IWebBlockInstanceWidget {source, empty}; create IWebEmail + set Subject"
   },
   "contract": [
    "verbs.verbs.create",
    "verbs.verbs.set",
    "verbs.verbs.link",
    "verbs.verbs.dump",
    "verbs.references"
   ],
   "depends": [],
   "alternatives": [],
   "guidance": "Choose Navigate for screen/URL destinations; Ajax (Ajax Submit) for same-screen actions, followed by explicit data fetching and Ajax Refresh of persistent containers; Submit for native upload/download. Ajax does not rerun screen Preparation. Use validation=None on tabs, pagination and modal open/close; retain server authorization for mutations. Explicit method/validation on button/a is supported; button with explicit policy becomes a styled native ILinkWidget because only ILinkOnClick exposes Method. Test browser behavior after publishing. A WebResponsive module supports new frontend documents through html data.html: <screen>/<block>, div/span, text/{{ expressions }}, input/textarea bind, button/a onclick destination, table/tr/td, Block/slot, div if/else/list and literal CSS. Declare screen actions as logic data.flow (action Screen.Name) in the same job; they run on the server. Proven example: traditional-html-frontend.json. The document creates IEntry only if none exists and preserves an existing default; never use ESpace.DefaultScreen for Traditional navigation. Existing roots use native @key edits: HTML editing, arbitrary JavaScript/React and screen generators remain outside this route. Queries use Preparation. Verify and merge do not prove server publication or resolve every ESpace.Dump failure.",
   "example": {
    "ops": [
     "create",
     "set",
     "link"
    ],
    "max": 24
   },
